      "text": "```python\nimport shlex\nimport subprocess\n\n_ALLOWED_COMMANDS = {\"pwd\", \"echo\"}\n_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 2\n\n\ndef execute_command(command: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Validate the command, execute it, and return its stdout as a string.\n\n    Only pwd and echo are supported; raise ValueError for any other command\n    or empty input. A two-second process timeout is applied.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(command, str):\n        raise ValueError(\"command must be a string\")\n\n    if not command.strip():\n        raise ValueError(\"command must not be empty\")\n\n    try:\n        tokens = shlex.split(command)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        raise ValueError(f\"invalid command syntax: {exc}\") from exc\n\n    if not tokens:\n        raise ValueError(\"command must not be empty\")\n\n    program = tokens[0]\n    if program not in _ALLOWED_COMMANDS:\n        raise ValueError(f\"unsupported command: {program!r}\")\n\n    if program == \"pwd\" and len(tokens) > 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"pwd does not accept arguments\")\n\n    result = subprocess.run(\n        tokens,\n        stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,\n        capture_output=True,\n        text=True,\n        timeout=_TIMEOUT_SECONDS,\n        check=False,\n    )\n\n    if result.returncode != 0:\n        raise RuntimeError(\n            f\"command {program!r} exited with status {result.returncode}: \"\n            f\"{result.stderr.strip()}\"\n        )\n\n    return result.stdout\n```",
